From 28a438edf88d63c15054ecaa2608298d0c0dbc3e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: P Arun Kumar Reddy <arunpapannagari23@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 16:02:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] libocp: add OCP Secure Firmware Recovery protocol library

Add a C++ static library implementing the recovery agent side of the
OCP Security WG "Secure Firmware Recovery" specification (v1.0
indirect-write path) over I2C/SMBus block transfers [1].

The library provides:
- The recovery command set: PROT_CAP, DEVICE_ID, DEVICE_STATUS,
  DEVICE_RESET (forced recovery), RECOVERY_CTRL, RECOVERY_STATUS,
  INDIRECT_CTRL, INDIRECT_STATUS and chunked INDIRECT_DATA writes.
  Every protocol code set (device status, recovery status, protocol
  errors, recovery reason codes, image selection, activation) is a
  distinct scoped enum so the overlapping numeric spaces cannot be
  mixed up.
- Single-transaction primitives that never sleep, so event-loop
  callers (sdbusplus::async coroutines) can own all polling delays.
  All fallible operations return std::expected values produced whole,
  only on success; transport failures carry the underlying errno.
- A blocking convenience layer (Target::writeImage/recover) for tests
  and standalone tooling.
- An abstract Transport interface; the built-in I2CTransport uses raw
  ioctl(I2C_RDWR) write/write+read messages and owns its fd. Unit
  tests drive the full protocol against a scripted mock transport,
  including wire-format goldens, chunking (252-byte blocks with
  acknowledge polling), vendor-length DEVICE_ID descriptors and error
  propagation.

Devices advertising only the v1.1 INDIRECT_FIFO mechanism are
rejected with std::errc::not_supported for now.

Tested: meson setup -Dtests=enabled && meson test (test_ocp_recovery,
26 cases).

[1] https://www.opencompute.org/documents/ocp-recovery-document-1p0-final-1-pdf

Change-Id: I64e72b1741fbe941ac95c08b23068fecbf47e473
Signed-off-by: P Arun Kumar Reddy <arunpapannagari23@gmail.com>

Upstream-Status: Submitted [https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/phosphor-bmc-code-mgmt/+/92450]
